{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W1MqXEAjGdnGVQghBZnB6K","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tCreated-Local: 2026-10-14 00:30 +07\n2\t# Task: slice 7d, Stage E on the semantic-register kernel (codex implements)\n3\t\n4\tWorktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7d`, branch `srvm-phase7d`, from the integration branch `srvm-phase7` (master + 7a custody on rows + 7b holder export/recovery v2/driver + 7c composition/fencing suites). This is the LAST slice of phase 7; when it is green on three hosts the integration branch goes to master. Your work will be reviewed by a NON-codex reviewer (Fable) with mutants. Read first: `docs/agents/build-n-test.md` (REMOTE servers section: shiva and jupiter, Node peer build, `npm ci` in a fresh worktree or the Node lane dies MODULE_NOT_FOUND; slow tier; the process matrix is about an hour per full pass on the remote hosts: you run JVM only and report what you could not run); `collab/phase7-plan.md` (section 1 inventory: every Stage E scenario and its parking shape; 3.4 crash cuts; 3.5 publication of successors; 3.6; section 4 slice 7d is your scope); `collab/7a-report.md`, `collab/1792480000000-engineer-7c-compose-fencing.report.md`, `collab/7c-review.md` (findings F1: add the `compose/open!` source-index refusal test beside `a-journal-substrate-is-checked-at-open-test` for both modes plus a non-fn `:source-index {}`; F3 below; F2/F4 optional doc nits: do F2 (name the suites in the `handoff_v2_authority_test` docstring)); `docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md` 7.11 and 7.7; the continuation design as amended; `test/yin/vm/ucf/stage_e_{world,scenarios,peer,rows_test,process_test}`, `compose_rows_test`, `rows_support`, `checkpoint_fixtures`. OWNER RULINGS: fork custody slot nil; the REPL custody gap accepted (you do NOT touch `yin.repl`); code and trees go through the composition's source-index (linker); A only code identity; BLAKE3; no compat shims or version dispatch; lease/epoch/holder never in a body; the de Bruijn kernels are backends, not Stage E participants, never widened; D2 of 7a is settled: `:yin.k/root` is in the baseline, so a re-emitted id-counter variant is a `:variant-conflict`; the only equal-baseline variant is the SAME root in another row order (reversed rows: other pack address, same root, same baseline): Stage E row-1 and `offer-variant!` must use that encoding (7c-review F3).\n5\tDo: port `stage_e_world.cljc` to the semantic-register kernel over `rows_support` (`parked-reader-over`, `reading-writer`; `holder-seams` supplies `:source-index`; `offer-variant!` re-emits the reversed-row pack; `snapshot`'s `:fences` reads pack digests); adjust `stage_e_scenarios.cljc` (checks that name `:yin.k/id-counter` or body keys; row 1's \"two encodings\" assertion keeps its meaning with the reversed-row encoding; the five currently red `stage-e-rows-test` cases: `row-1-candidates-and-encodings-test`, `row-7-failure-lower-and-lost-authority-test`, `row-3-reclaim-test`, `fork-per-host-test`, `row-5-replay-divergence-test` fail only because the world supplies no source index); `stage_e_peer.cljc`, `stage_e_process_test.clj`, `stage_e_rows_test.cljc` only if needed (the Node peer build picks up the new namespaces: check the Node peer entry namespace list/regexp and update it if it names old fixtures). Acceptance (plan 7d): `stage_e_rows_test` green on JVM (slow tier with `DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1`), and written so it runs on Node and Dart; `stage_e_process_test` JVM-driven over `[[:jvm :jvm] [:jvm :node] [:node :jvm] [:node :node]]` with every cut a SIGKILL: you CANNOT run it fully: run the fast-lane gate `the-cross-host-handoff-across-processes-test` on the JVM pair if your sandbox allows processes and report; the orchestrator runs the Node/process matrix on shiva and jupiter. Row 10's canonical-byte agreement across hosts holds for packs (sorted rows): keep or add the assertion. All of `yin.vm.ucf.*` green after this slice (list anything red). Also land F1, F2. Portability: `.cljc` JVM/Node/Dart (no `for` over possibly long seqs, no private var access, `(assoc {} ...)`, no unary minus on floats, `#?(:cljd nil :clj ...)` order, catches `#?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default)`, no EDN strings with whitespace before closers). If the plan and the code disagree, the code wins: report design defects, never silently change semantics. Verification, foreground only, JVM: `clj -M:kondo --lint <changed files>`; `clojure -M:test -e :slow -n <each touched ns>`, `-i :slow` with `DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1`; every `yin.vm.ucf.*` namespace; `rows_test`, harness, layout unchanged. Mutants (cp backup; diff and `git diff --quiet` to verify): fence omitted from a world step; variant offered with the counter-changed encoding accepted as equal-baseline; successor published before the fence; lost-authority check skipped; a crash cut that never fires (assert each cut fires); report accepting an unfenced result; per-host fork divergence ignored. Which does your suite catch? Do not commit. Report `collab/1792500000000-engineer-7d-stage-e.report.md`: files and line counts, test counts, mutants, what you could not run, deviations, design defects, what 7e docs need to state.\n6\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c88f8d87-995f-4b00-89ec-984c8c9878f0","uuid":"fe11132f-0651-4670-8902-798d1a32d03c","timestamp":"2026-10-13T18:37:33.766Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7d/collab/1792500000000-engineer-7d-stage-e.prompt.md","content":"Created-Local: 2026-10-14 00:30 +07\n# Task: slice 7d, Stage E on the semantic-register kernel (codex implements)\n\nWorktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7d`, branch `srvm-phase7d`, from the integration branch `srvm-phase7` (master + 7a custody on rows + 7b holder export/recovery v2/driver + 7c composition/fencing suites). This is the LAST slice of phase 7; when it is green on three hosts the integration branch goes to maste