{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DExrSD3B9sDihmZnGBVsUV","type":"tool_result","content":";; shadow-cljs configuration\n;; Source paths come from deps.edn (:paths plus the :cljs alias's\n;; :extra-paths); shadow ignores any :source-paths set here when :deps\n;; is used.\n{:deps {:aliases [:cljs]}\n\n :dev-http {9000 \"public\"}\n\n :builds {:demo {:target :browser\n                 :devtools {:use-document-protocol true}\n                 :modules {:main {:init-fn datomworld.demo/init}}}\n\n          :local {:target :browser\n                  :devtools {:use-document-protocol true}\n                  :closure-defines {datomworld.demo/WEBSOCKET_PORT 8090}\n                  :modules {:main {:init-fn datomworld.demo/init}}}\n\n          :test {:target :node-test\n                 :output-to \"target/node-tests.js\"\n                 :autorun true}\n\n          :vm-bench {:target :node-script\n                     :main bench.yin-vm-bench/-main\n                     :output-to \"target/vm-bench.js\"}\n\n          :yin-repl {:target :node-script\n                        :main yin.repl.main/-main\n                        :output-to \"target/yin-repl.js\"}}}\n----\n6:   own operating-system process (yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-peer) over the\n7:   scenario's durable file media, each cut a real kill: the peer prints\n13:   The Node peer is required: it is compiled here, before the first\n14:   Node life (shadow-cljs's :vm-bench node-script build with the peer as\n15:   its main, to target/stage-e-peer.js), so this gate cannot skip; a\n16:   failed build fails the test.  The JVM peer runs from classes this\n49:;; The peers\n53:(def ^:private node-peer \"target/stage-e-peer.js\")\n70:    (run-build! \"Node peer\"\n71:                [\"clj\" \"-M:cljs\" \"-m\" \"shadow.cljs.devtools.cli\" \"compile\" \"vm-bench\"\n72:                 \"--config-merge\"\n73:                 (str \"{:main yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-peer/main :output-to \\\"\" node-peer \"\\\"}\")])\n74:    (when-not (.exists (io/file node-peer))\n75:      (throw (ex-info \"stage E: the Node peer build wrote nothing\" {:path node-peer})))\n87:    (run-build! \"JVM peer classes\"\n90:                 \"clojure.main\" \"-e\"\n92:                      \" (compile 'yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-peer))\")])\n102:              \"clojure.main\" \"-m\" \"yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-peer\" spec-path])\n104:              [\"node\" node-peer spec-path])))\n143:  \"Run one life of `spec` as a peer process on `host`: answer the same\n169:              (throw (ex-info \"stage E: a peer ended without a report\"\n186:                  :error (throw (ex-info (str \"stage E: a peer failed: \" (:message e))\n----\n16:bb test:cljs         # Node (shadow-cljs :cljs alias), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\n29:# On Node, shadow also runs the test namespaces those nine require (about\n62:# Cross-host peers the JVM lane spawns. `bb test` builds both. A bare\n64:# without build:yin-repl-peer first, the Dart-peer tests skip with a printed notice.\n66:bb build:yin-repl-peer   # Dart exe build/yin-repl-peer (yin.repl R5 pairs)\n88:change (deps.edn bb.edn shadow-cljs.edn mise.toml .cljstyle src/dev/\n93:and spawned programs that changed (target/yin-repl.js, Dart peers).\n120:Prerequisites (`build:yin-repl-peer`, `build:yin-repl-node`, `gen:python-antlr`)\n147:  exists to spawn. `build/yin-repl-peer` is the R5 slice peer, not a\n151:# ClojureScript / shadow-cljs (always via deps.edn :cljs alias, never npx)\n152:clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli watch <build-id>    # e.g. watch demo\n153:clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile <build-id>  # e.g. compile demo\n154:clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli release <build-id>  # production release\n167:with its dots already escaped for an EDN string (bb.edn feeds it to shadow-cljs\n352:find flutter on PATH\", and so does `bb build:yin-repl-peer`.\n370:- **JVM and Node may share a clone.** Node writes `target/` and `.shadow-cljs/`; the\n406:bb build:yin-repl-peer >\"$LOG/build-peer.log\" 2>&1 && echo \"dart peer built $(ts)\" | tee -a \"$LOG/summary.txt\"  # shiva only\n410:lane node clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile test &\n413:    bb build:yin-repl-peer >\"$LOG/build-peer-dart.log\" 2>&1\n440:- A JVM lane started before the Dart peer is built skips the Dart-peer tests with a\n441:  printed notice. The script builds the peer first so they run.\n449:Node REPL, ANTLR) took about 30 s; the Dart peer 91 s. JVM and Node lane times are\n485:4. **After brackets balance**, rerun `clj-kondo`, then rebuild with `clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile <build>`.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c88f8d87-995f-4b00-89ec-984c8c9878f0","uuid":"6c1aa9f5-b818-4077-87f8-3d39162e7d93","timestamp":"2026-10-13T18:37:53.277Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":";; shadow-cljs configuration\n;; Source paths come from deps.edn (:paths plus the :cljs alias's\n;; :extra-paths); shadow ignores any :source-paths set here when :deps\n;; is used.\n{:deps {:aliases [:cljs]}\n\n :dev-http {9000 \"public\"}\n\n :builds {:demo {:target :browser\n                 :devtools {:use-document-protocol true}\n                 :modules {:main {:init-fn datomworld.demo/init}}}\n\n          :local {:target :browser\n                  :devtools {:use-document-protocol true}\n                  :closure-defines {datomworld.demo/WEBSOCKET_PORT 8090}\n                  :modules {:main {:init-fn datomworld.demo/init}}}\n\n          :test {:target :node-test\n                 :output-to \"target/node-tests.js\"\n                 :autorun true}\n\n          :vm-bench {:target :node-script\n                     :main bench.yin-vm-bench/-main\n                     :output-to \"target/vm-bench.js\"}\n\n          :yin-repl {:target :node-script\n                        :main yin.repl.main/-main\n                        :output-to \"target/yin-repl.js\"}}}\n----\n6:   own operating-system process (yin.vm.ucf.