{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EsX9N86nv6Hi19qyfqujLb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yin.vm.ucf.compose-test\n2\t  \"D15: the composition (r3 1.5, 1.11 and the D15 test contract).  A\n3\t   file-backed journal substrate -- backends whose declaration covers\n4\t   :process-crash -- carries every exclusive row, beside the file-backed\n5\t   authority that passes `authority/exclusive-capable?`; the memory\n6\t   substrate stays the fork's, and the substrate gate rows refuse every\n7\t   exclusive composition that would journal to less than its declared\n8\t   failure model.  Every authority, judge, front and holder below is the\n9\t   landed one, composed; this namespace requires no yin.repl namespace,\n10\t   which the subprocess row proves on the JVM for load and drive alike.\"\n11\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n12\t            [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n13\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n14\t            [dao.stream.journal :as journal]\n15\t            [dao.stream.journal.file :as file-journal]\n16\t            [dao.stream.memory-log :as memory-log]\n17\t            #?@(:cljd [[\"dart:io\" :as dart-io]]\n18\t                :clj [[clojure.java.io :as io]])\n19\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n20\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n21\t            [yin.vm.ucf.authority :as authority]\n22\t            [yin.vm.ucf.compose :as compose]\n23\t            [yin.vm.ucf.rows-support :as s]))\n24\t\n25\t\n26\t;; =============================================================================\n27\t;; The substrate: integer-position streams, attach tables, machines\n28\t;; =============================================================================\n29\t\n30\t\n31\t(defn- int-stream\n32\t  \"A stream whose values sit in an atom and whose cursors are plain\n33\t   integer positions, so a position lifted from the source's instance is\n34\t   a valid cursor on the receiving composition's own instance.\"\n35\t  [identity]\n36\t  (let [values (atom [])]\n37\t    (reify\n38\t      stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n39\t      (descriptor\n40\t        [_]\n41\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n42\t         :dao.stream/identity identity\n43\t         :dao.stream/descriptor {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n44\t                                 :dao.stream/identity identity}})\n45\t\n46\t\n47\t      stream/IDaoStreamReader\n48\t\n49\t      (cursor\n50\t        [_ _anchor]\n51\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/cursor 0})\n52\t\n53\t      (next\n54\t        [_ cursor]\n55\t        (let [vs @values]\n56\t          (cond\n57\t            (not (and (integer? cursor) (<= 0 cursor (count vs))))\n58\t            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-cursor}\n59\t            (< cursor (count vs))\n60\t            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c88f8d87-995f-4b00-89ec-984c8c9878f0","uuid":"fadef1f5-5803-40a9-b17e-107f6bacf8e3","timestamp":"2026-10-13T18:38:18.727Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7d/test/yin/vm/ucf/compose_test.cljc","content":"(ns yin.vm.ucf.compose-test\n  \"D15: the composition (r3 1.5, 1.11 and the D15 test contract).  A\n   file-backed journal substrate -- backends whose declaration covers\n   :process-crash -- carries every exclusive row, beside the file-backed\n   authority that passes `authority/exclusive-capable?`; the memory\n   substrate stays the fork's, and the substrate gate rows refuse every\n   exclusive composition that would journal to less than its declared\n   failure model.  Every authority, judge, front and holder below is the\n   landed one, composed; this namespace requires no yin.repl namespace,\n   which the subprocess row proves on the JVM for load and drive alike.\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.journal :as journal]\n            [dao.stream.journal.file :as file-journal]\n            [dao.stream.memory-log :as memory-log]\n            #?@(:cljd [[\"dart:io\" :as dart-io]]\n                :clj [[clojure.java.io :as io]])\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.authority :as authority]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.compose :as compose]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows-support :as s]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The substrate: integer-position streams, attach tables, machines\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(defn- int-stream\n  \"A stream whose values sit in an atom and whose cursors are plain\n   integer positions, so a position lifted from the source's instance is\n   a valid cursor on the receiving composition's own instance.\"\n  [identity]\n  (let [values (atom [])]\n    (reify\n      stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n      (descriptor\n        [_]\n        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n         :dao.stream/identity identity\n         :dao.stream/descriptor {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n                                 :dao.stream/identity identity}})\n\n\n      stream/IDaoStreamReader\n\n      (cursor\n        [_ _anchor]\n        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/cursor 0})\n\n      (next\n        [_ cursor]\n        (let [vs @values]\n          (cond\n            (not (and (integer? cursor) (<= 0 cursor (count vs))))\n            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-cursor}\n            (< cursor (count vs))\n            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1140}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EsX9N86nv6Hi19qyfqujLb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
