{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019doCxK1UF6Hg5Cx7gMgTEK","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7d/collab/1792510000000-review-7d-stage-e.findings.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c88f8d87-995f-4b00-89ec-984c8c9878f0","uuid":"99f7c092-c213-4dec-93f9-2b6dbb84223e","timestamp":"2026-10-13T18:49:36.314Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7d/collab/1792510000000-review-7d-stage-e.findings.md","content":"Created-Local: 2026-10-14 +07\n# Review findings: slice 7d, Stage E on the semantic-register kernel\n\nReviewer: claude-fable-5-1 (non-author; codex wrote 7d). Worktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7d`, branch `srvm-phase7d`, commit `8aa148be` over `srvm-phase7` (7a, 7b, 7c merged). Method: full read of `git diff srvm-phase7..HEAD` (four test files, no production change, confirmed by `--stat`), the brief, codex's report, `7c-review.md`, the plan (§1.1, §3.3-3.6, slice 7d); the whole of `stage_e_scenarios.cljc` and the touched regions of `stage_e_world.cljc`, the process harness's result shape and the peer's event printing; the production seams the new assertions lean on (`rows/pack`, `rows/decode`, `rows/pack-address`, `rows/custody-baseline`, `rows.checkpoint/inspect`, `compose/check-common!`, `driver/export-fence-step`, `completion/successor-defect`); the quick and slow lanes; one throwaway probe; 13 mutants of my own with byte-level restore. JVM only (Node/Dart by reading). Nothing in the repo edited (the probe namespace was deleted after its run); artifacts under `target/7d-review/` (ignored).\n\n## Verification I ran\n\n| Lane | Command | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Quick, every UCF ns | `clojure -M:test -e :slow -r 'yin\\.vm\\.ucf\\..*'` (foreground, `target/7d-review/ucf-quick.log`) | 701 tests, 9452 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors. Matches codex. The five Stage E cases red in 7c are green. |\n| Slow, Stage E rows | `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-rows-test` (`target/7d-review/stage-e-slow.log`) | 8 tests, 632 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors. Matches codex. Run without the `DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1` prefix: the sandbox would not let me pass the variable, and `dao.test-slow/enabled?` is `true` on the JVM unconditionally (`test/dao/test_slow.cljc:17`), so the two invocations are identical there (as noted in 7c-review). |\n| Lint | `clj -M:kondo --lint` the four files | 0 errors, 0 warnings |\n| Whitespace | `git diff --check srvm-phase7..HEAD` | clean |\n| Probe | row 1 in process (`target/7d-review/probe.log`) | the `:race` snapshot's `:packs` holds one entry (the fenced pack), `:final` one; `:packs` and `:variant-baseline` are plain data (`(= x (->data x))`), so the row-1 baseline comparison is a real comparison on the process transport too; the occurrence shows exactly two variant addresses. |\n| Restore | `git diff --quiet -- src test`, `git status --short -- src test` after the mutant pass | clean |\n\nNot run (by instruction): the process matrix, the Node peer compile, Node/Dart in-process Stage E.\n\n## Item by item\n\n1. **Every Stage E scenario still runs and asserts what it asserted.** The diff touches one check only: row 1 (`stage_e_scenarios.cljc:706-723`), where `(val (first running))` became `(second (first running))` (nil-safe, same value) and a block was added that pins the two encodings as distinct pack addresses with identical inspected baselines; the old assertions (one running holder, every competitor awaits or refused, two variants, one live lease, two attaches, the source resumes under its own grant) are all still there. Row 7's five cuts, failure-lower and lost-authority (`:1239-1309`), rows 4/3/5, the fork row, row 2's fourteen cuts and four carrier outcomes, rows 6, clause 8, clause 3 and the journal rows are byte-identical to `srvm-phase7`. Nothing vacuous found: every cut-bearing scenario asserts `(:killed? l1)` and the cut name; the lost-authority refusal is asserted with its kind (`:yin.k/unsatisfied`/`:authority-refused` or the backend's `:transport-error`); the new runner assertion (`:71-75`) requires `:killed?` and exactly one `:cut` event naming the requested cut, and applies equally to the process harness, whose result carries `:events` from the peer's printed events and `:killed? true` only on a `:cut` event (`stage_e_process_test.clj:175-185`). Lives that `:die` carry no `:cut`, so the assertion is skipped for them, correctly. My T2 (the `:row7/while-running` predicate never matches) trips both runner assertions plus the scenario's own.\n2. **`:packs` and the Row 10 re-emission (`stage_e_world.cljc:981-993`, `stage_e_scenarios.cljc:76-82`).** For every `:yin.k/fenced` record the stored bytes are decoded, inspected, checked for sorted row ids on the **stored** wire, and re-emitted on this host through `rows/decode` → `rows/emit` → `cbor/encode`; the runner compares that digest with `:fences`' digest of the stored bytes, so the assertion is on the exact canonical bytes, not on a self-comparison. The fenced record's `:yin.k/address` is the pack (the recovery object is `:yin.k/record`, `driver.cljc:916-919`), so the recovery object never enters `:packs`. The reversed-row variant is offered, never fenced, so it is excluded by construction (probe: one pack, two variants). On the process matrix the receiver life reads h1's durable fence and re-emits the source host's bytes: the cross-host claim is real there and only there, as codex says. Teeth: T1 (re-emit digest from reversed rows) fails 4 assertions in row 7 failure-lower; P6 (`pack` stops sorting) fails `:sorted?` 4 times.\n3. **F1 and F2 landed.** `compose_test.cljc:682-697`: both modes × {absent, `{}`}, `thrown-with-msg?` on `\"source index\"`, which is `check-common!`'s message (`compose.cljc:188-189`); P7 (the `check!` removed) fails all four. Note th