nged in 7d and none of my mutants found a production defect. The owner's rulings hold in the tests as written: A names code and trees come only through the composition's source index (both `open!` sites, P7), the pack address is the store key and the root the semantic identity (T5, T6, P5), the only equal-baseline variant is the same root in another row order (T5), BLAKE3 throughout (`pack-address`, `digest-of`), no version dispatch or shim, lease/epoch/holder outside the body, `yin.repl` untouched, the de Bruijn kernels untouched. Codex's three deviations are all stale plan text, not code defects, and match 7c-review F3.\n\nVERDICT: READY_TO_MERGE (into the integration branch `srvm-phase7`). F1 is a one-line portability hedge decided by the orchestrator's Dart lane; everything else is informational. Tri-host acceptance of phase 7 still waits on the orchestrator's Node/Dart in-process runs and the four-pair process matrix on shiva/jupiter, as the brief assigns.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019doCxK1UF6Hg5Cx7gMgTEK","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
