{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011Cfzjjb13Jwuhj7ZVqHQKD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review done. Findings written to `collab/1792510000000-review-7d-stage-e.findings.md`.\n\n**Verdict: READY_TO_MERGE** into `srvm-phase7`.\n\nWhat I verified:\n- Quick lane: 701 tests, 9452 assertions, 0/0. Slow Stage E lane: 8 tests, 632 assertions, 0/0. Lint and whitespace clean. The `DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1` prefix was refused by the sandbox, but it is a no-op on the JVM, so the run is identical.\n- Every Stage E scenario is byte-identical to the integration branch except row 1, which keeps its old assertions and gains the reversed-row baseline comparison. The new runner assertions have teeth: a cut predicate that never fires trips both of them.\n- The `:packs` observation is non-vacuous. A probe showed one fenced pack per snapshot, plain data across the process transport, and the variant excluded by construction. Wrong re-emission and an unsorted `pack` both fail.\n- Node peer: the `:vm-bench` main is overridden by `--config-merge`, no allowlist exists, and every new transitive require is a `.cljc` on the cljs paths. Compile not run, per the brief.\n- 13 mutants, all restored byte-for-byte. Eleven are killed. Two survive Stage E alone (recovery stored after the pack, origin check removed) and are killed by the Stage D/C suites that own them, as the plan intends.\n\nOne finding worth acting on: F1, low. The `:sorted?` check sorts row-id keywords with the default comparator, which I could not verify on ClojureDart. A one-line `sort-by str` mirrors how `rows/pack` already orders ids. The orchestrator's Dart run decides whether it is needed.\n\nOne housekeeping note: a mid-run driver fix interrupted one mutant, and I restored `driver.cljc` from its byte backup before the rerun. The driver's final pass confirmed `git diff --quiet -- src test` is clean, and the probe namespace was deleted. My last standalone status check was blocked by the sandbox, so the final state rests on that driver output."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":156,"cache_read_input_tokens":212851,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":156},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c88f8d87-995f-4b00-89ec-984c8c9878f0","uuid":"fc0c752b-6ec5-4294-8573-c87f03bc3ae6","timestamp":"2026-10-13T18:49:51.076Z","request_id":"req_011CfzjjafhYmZDJv3vrCm7g"}
